@startuml
title C4 Level 2 — Container Diagram\nMeeting Room Booking System

left to right direction

skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam nodesep 65
skinparam ranksep 55
skinparam rectangle {
    Padding 15
}

actor "Employee" as Employee
actor "Administrator" as Admin

rectangle "Meeting Room Booking System" {
    rectangle "Web Frontend\n[HTML, CSS, JavaScript]\nEmployee and administrator UI" as Frontend

    rectangle "Backend API\n[Python, FastAPI]\nREST API, demo authentication,\nbusiness rules and audit logging" as Backend

    rectangle "Outbox Publisher\n[Python worker]\nPublishes pending booking events" as Publisher

    rectangle "Email Worker\n[Python worker]\nConsumes events and sends email" as Worker
}

database "PostgreSQL\n[Neon]\nUsers, rooms, bookings,\naudit log and outbox events" as DB

queue "RabbitMQ\n[Message broker]\nBooking events, email queue and DLQ" as RabbitMQ

rectangle "Email Provider\n[SMTP / UniSender Go API]" as Email <<External System>>

Employee --> Frontend : Uses booking features\n[HTTPS]
Admin --> Frontend : Uses administration features\n[HTTPS]

Frontend --> Backend : Calls REST API\n[JSON/HTTPS]
Backend --> DB : Reads and writes application data;\nstores booking and outbox event\nin one transaction [SQL]

Publisher --> DB : Polls PENDING outbox events [SQL]
Publisher --> RabbitMQ : Publishes booking.created,\nbooking.updated and booking.cancelled [AMQP]
RabbitMQ --> Worker : Delivers notification events [AMQP]
Worker --> DB : Loads user, room and office context [SQL]
Worker --> Email : Sends notification [SMTP]

Backend --> Email : Sends notification directly\nin the serverless deployment [HTTPS]

note bottom of Backend
  The current public demo uses role-based Demo Auth.
  Corporate authentication is a planned replacement.
end note

note bottom of RabbitMQ
  The asynchronous RabbitMQ path is optional locally.
  The Vercel deployment uses direct UniSender API delivery.
end note

@enduml
